{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1364","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. X-OR"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem!"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ehab has a hidden permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$ consisting of the elements from $$$0$$$ to $$$n-1$$$. You, for some reason, want to figure out the permutation. To do that, you can give Ehab $$$2$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"different"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" indices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$, and he'll reply with $$$(p_i|p_j)$$$ where $$$|$$$ is the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#OR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise-or"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ehab has just enough free time to answer $$$4269$$$ questions, and while he's OK with answering that many questions, he's too lazy to play your silly games, so he'll fix the permutation beforehand and will "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" change it depending on your queries. Can you guess the permutation?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains the integer $$$n$$$ $$$(3 \\le n \\le 2048)$$$ — the length of the permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To ask a question, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? $$$i$$$ $$$j$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes, $$$i \\neq j$$$) Then, you should read the answer, which will be $$$(p_i|p_j)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If we answer with $$$-1$$$ instead of a valid answer, that means you exceeded the number of queries or made an invalid query."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Exit immediately after receiving $$$-1$$$ and you will see "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"wrong answer"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" verdict. Otherwise, you can get an arbitrary verdict because your solution will continue to read from a closed stream."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To print the answer, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"! $$$p_1$$$ $$$p_2$$$ $$$\\ldots$$$ $$$p_n$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes). "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that answering doesn't count as one of the $$$4269$$$ queries"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After printing a query or printing the answer, do not forget to output end of line and flush the output. Otherwise, you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, use:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Java;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Pascal;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" See the documentation for other languages."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacks:"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line should contain the integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 2^{11}$$$) — the length of the permutation $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line should contain $$$n$$$ space-separated integers $$$p_1$$$, $$$p_2$$$, $$$\\ldots$$$, $$$p_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le p_i \\lt n$$$) — the elements of the permutation $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1\n3\n2"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n? 1 2\n? 1 3\n? 2 3\n! 1 0 2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, the permutation is $$$[1,0,2]$$$. You start by asking about $$$p_1|p_2$$$ and Ehab replies with $$$1$$$. You then ask about $$$p_1|p_3$$$ and Ehab replies with $$$3$$$. Finally, you ask about $$$p_2|p_3$$$ and Ehab replies with $$$2$$$. You then guess the permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1364E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1364/problem/E"}